<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ohkay Owingeh</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as San Juan Pueblo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ohkay Owingeh, formerly San Juan Pueblo, is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tewa">Tewa</a> pueblo on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande">Rio Grande</a> north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santa-fe-new-mexico">Santa Fe, New Mexico</a>. In 1598 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-de-onate">Juan de Oñate</a> made it the first headquarters of the Spanish colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-mexico">New Mexico</a>, naming it San Juan de los Caballeros. It was the home of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope">Popé</a>, the religious leader who organised the Pueblo Revolt of 1680, and it restored its original Tewa name in 2005.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ohkay-owingeh.jpg" alt="Ohkay Owingeh" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Davidhc9 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:San_Juan_Bautista_Church_at_Ohkay_Owingeh_Pueblo.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
